<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11542" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαρν-έομαι</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					461c
				</span></i>
			: aor.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπηρνησάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Cer.</u>
					75
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				107
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.1133
			</span></i> (v.l.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				16.24
			</span></i>, al., but in Trag. and 
				Att.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ηρνήθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					480
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				1266
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.56
			</span></i>, etc.:—<i>deny utterly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.69
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλέψαντες ἀπαρνεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					2.3.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή . . ἀπαρνηθεὶς γένῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Sph.</u>
					217c
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαρνηθῆναί τι</span>
			<i>to refuse, reject</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
			</span></i> l.c., etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. μή</span> c.
				inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν . . ἀπαρνηθέντα μὴ χρᾶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀπαρνοῦμαι τὸ
			μή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρᾶσαι</span>) <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				443
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Aj.</u>
				96
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίνα οἴει ἀπαρνήσεσθαι μὴ οὐ . .;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					461c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷός ἐστι μὴ ἂν ἀ. χαρίσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					256a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in Logic, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατηγορεῖν,</span>
			<i>deny,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APr.</u>
				41a9
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				63b37
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἑαυτόν</span>
			<i>deny</i> oneself, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				16.24
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαρνηθήσεται</span> it <i>shall be
				denied</i> or <i>refused,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				527
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				12.9
			</span></i>, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Is.</u>
				31.7
			</span></i>: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥνθρωπος ἓν μὲν οἶδεν, ἓν δ᾽
					ἀπηρνήθη</span>”
				<i>was refused,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herod.
					4.74
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
